WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.167
Israel has been

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.536
known as the stable democracy

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.038
in the Middle East.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.874
It has also been home to the growing

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.143
and extremely important global

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.778
tech sector.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.413
Many of the technologies

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.483
that we use today came from Israel,

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.685
which is why the latest

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.487
protests in the street

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.622
over the new judicial reforms

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.357
is so serious.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.259
In many cases, people are saying

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.961
that the very fabric of the country

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.397
is at stake.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.033
Two months of protests on the streets

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.134
of Israel

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.101
with the demonstrators

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.668
coming from

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.804
all corners of Israeli society

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.807
and as a growing fear.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.410
Democratic values are under threat.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.112
An unprecedented overhaul

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.248
of the Israeli legal system

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.649
could dramatically shrink

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.684
the powers of the Supreme Court

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.587
and hand sweeping new authority

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.855
to the Knesset.

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.157
Israel's parliament

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.592
sets out to limit York

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.960
The new rules would prevent

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.928
the Supreme Court

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.731
justices from striking down legislation

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.933
passed by lawmakers.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.435
The rules would change the way

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.203
judges are selected,

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.505
giving more power to politicians.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.075
And it would allow for a simple majority

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.944
in the Knesset to overturn rulings

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.045
from the court

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.981
Bibi Miller, she said.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.216
Behind the plan

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.086
is a new ultra right coalition government

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.854
led by longstanding

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:30.190
prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.193
The prime minister has tried to frame

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.227
this plan

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.896
as mere constitutional housekeeping,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.966
making things better Israel's long

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.836
standing commitment to liberal values

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.304
and the rule of law

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:44.671
has helped

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.572
the country attract

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.007
many billions of dollars of investment

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.176
from Western companies.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.012
The country's far right finance minister

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.381
says that judicial reforms

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.817
will attract even more investment.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.651
However,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.086
one of Israel's former

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:00.987
central bank

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:03.590
governors strongly disagrees

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.191
with that proposal.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.560
I look at Poland, I look at Hungary,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.796
I look much more extreme.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.232
Turkey everywhere.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:15.168
Well, the judicial system has weakened

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.805
economic performance has weakened

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.974
foreign investment as decline.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.577
Doubts about Israel's economic future

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.212
appear to be growing.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.448
The shekel has already fallen sharply

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.116
as credit agencies

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.685
warn Israel's rating could suffer.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:33.820
And leaders

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:34.754
in the tech sector

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.323
fear investment could move elsewhere.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.826
Despite all this opposition,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.462
the government here is forging ahead

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.998
and hoping to pass the new laws

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.333
by Passover next month.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.070
Now to

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.641
Israel's current central bank governor,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.210
who tells me that the independence

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.745
of the judiciary

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.447
is imperative and essential.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.584
I spoke to Governor Amir Yaron

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.818
because, of course,

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:09.289
if judicial independence is up for grabs,

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.090
then I of course, I wanted to know

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.193
whether central bank independence

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.195
would also be up for grabs.

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.296
The governor has been

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.164
critical of the reforms

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.133
and he hasn't changed his views.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.034
Right now,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.770
the changes in the judicial reform

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:28.641
could weaken some of this independence.

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.510
Moreover,

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:34.113
the process itself is hasty one,

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:38.251
and that does not have a wide agreement

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.286
in the public. Do you fear?

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.121
And of course, on this program tonight,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.190
we will hear investors

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.491
in the tech industry,

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.627
which is a huge part of the economy here,

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.363
basically saying we will withdraw.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.398
We will disinvest.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.933
We have seen

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.468
some high tech leaders

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.636
and industry leaders

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.972
telling us that maybe investment firms

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.006
won't come in

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.075
and some of them are even talking that

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.011
they might take their business elsewhere

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.346
in the long run.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.615
The implication might be

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:11.084
basically brain drain, etc..

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.752
And this is why this

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.321
needs to be handled with care.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.523
This has huge implications.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.760
And this is why, again, it's imperative

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.262
that we maintain

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.663
the strength and independent

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:24.631
of this institution.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.798
And this is done

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.133
in a way that is

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.936
has a wide acceptance in the public.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.071
And it's a transparent process.

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.306
You keep talking about

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.308
the institutional aspect

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.142
and the independence

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.377
of the institutional aspect.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.947
That suggests

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.714
to someone like me

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.550
you're basically worried you're next.

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:45.752
So do you fear that

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.287
your independence is under

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.655
could be under threat?

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:50.423
I cannot be clearer than this.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.358
The independence of the governor,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.527
the independence of the central bank

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.096
are critical to the economy.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:59.399
Any country that has tinkered,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.401
let alone weakened,

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.935
the independence of the central

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.671
bank, has suffered dire

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.873
economic consequences.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:09.275
I believe all our leaders

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.110
and decision makers

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.913
ultimately understands this and therefore

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.214
would not come close

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.083
to touching the independence of the bank.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:17.884
You understand it

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:19.619
or you hope it, Richard.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.553
The proof

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.220
in the pudding

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.623
is the prime minister himself

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.625
and also the finance minister.

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.026
Immediately

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:29.429
when these issues came up, stated

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.830
very clearly

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.266
that only the governor decides

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.034
on the interest rates

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:37.203
and the central bank independence

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.572
is central bank independence.

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:41.040
Let's talk about the economy.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.242
It's pretty robust.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:46.112
It's good you're raising rates

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.148
Have you revised your terminal rate?

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:50.083
Israel

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:53.486
has had a great economic performance

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:54.954
in the last couple of years.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.890
We've grown 8.6% in 21

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:02.061
and 6.6 and a half percent in 20, 22.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:06.265
And we're on a way to 3% during 20, 23.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.067
And the hope is to go back to three

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.370
and a half percent in 20, 24.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.404
I should give the government

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:12.238
lots of credit.

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:14.140
It just passed a budget

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.377
that was moderate, was not expansionary.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.912
Moreover, public wages

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.515
were done in in a way

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.851
that was also modest and not expansion.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.285
I think what we are seeing

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.088
everywhere is the stickiness of inflation

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:32.291
that is especially in services.

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:34.594
So we are determined

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:36.262
absolutely determined

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.330
to bring inflation

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.332
back down to its target.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:40.299
And if that means

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.168
continuing raising rates

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:44.504
and that is our primary tool

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.972
that's what we will do.

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:49.142
The reality of what you have just said

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:52.745
and the sticky notes of inflation.

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:55.348
Are you surprised that central bankers

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:56.816
don't really understand

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.384
why they're not seeing a more of

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.886
a response?

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:02.955
I think all central banks or many central

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.991
banks are facing this stickiness.

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:05.558
It's partly

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:07.627
goes back to the exit of COVID,

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:08.895
to the facts,

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.464
to the fact that there were vast fiscal

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:13.633
stimulus in Israel.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:15.568
It wasn't as big as in the US,

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:17.804
but we have a thriving economy,

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.605
partly because of what I said

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.007
in the high tech sector

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:23.109
that allows for more consumption

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.378
and for more people's spending.

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:26.779
We we're also seeing some shifts

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:30.183
in the labor market, and that means

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:31.784
that it will take a little bit

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.786
more pain, probably

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:36.856
in order to bring inflation back down

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.524
to its target.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:41.761
But at what point do you decide, wow,

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.896
we're close enough to the target,

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:46.132
we're left with pivot?

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.533
Is pivoting dangerous?

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.769
I think pivoting is dangerous.

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:50.770
We know

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:52.572
and there is experience in the past

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:54.474
that if you stop too early,

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.742
inflation can come back with a vengeance.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.846
And therefore, I predict that

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:01.113
at least around the world,

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.282
we will see rates continue to go up

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.284
and they will stay up

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.420
for quite a bit longer.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.655
Is this the most difficult

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.557
of economic scenarios?

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.526
Our job is difficult.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:15.127
It is to manage the economy.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:15.795
The job

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:18.631
to take inflation down today, it's

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:20.500
it involves pain.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:21.200
And in Israel,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.602
it involves direct pain

00:08:22.602 --> 00:08:24.370
because many of the mortgages

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.272
are tied down directly

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:28.007
to the central bank interest rate.

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.542
You've got a lot on your plate,

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:30.042
haven't you?

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.310
I mean, you really have.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.912
It's it's not easy.

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:34.413
What do you do to switch off

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:36.549
on a personal.

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:37.884
Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:37.884 --> 00:08:39.118
Do you switch off?

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.854
First of all, this is a 20 47 job.

00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:45.691
Richard, just if you look at my terms

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:48.327
so far, I had five elections for

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:49.862
prime ministers,

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.798
for finance minister Pandemia.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.868
We had a mini war here.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.370
We, of course,

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.938
Ukraine, Russia, inflation.

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:01.440
So the plate is full.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.943
My basically people know

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:05.845
I love to run on the beach

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:09.849
and I invite everyone abroad to come in

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:12.552
and see the beautiful beaches in Israel

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:14.153
with me.

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:15.187
It's Hudachko

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:17.823
who is our correspondent in Israel.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:20.860
He does when I listen to the governor

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:23.429
and I also think about the other issues,

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:24.797
for example,

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:27.600
the settlements, the violence over that,

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:29.735
the expansion of the Jewish settlements

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:30.903
that dozens of people

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.305
who have been killed.

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:34.106
One gets this feeling of a country

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:35.541
almost falling apart.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:37.643
It is incredible to think of all the

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:38.911
massive fronts

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:40.346
that this country is already facing.

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:42.782
Not only on the internal domestic issues,

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:44.183
but then, of course,

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.152
with the Israeli-Palestinian conflict

00:09:46.152 --> 00:09:48.054
that's been rearing its head, really.

00:09:48.054 --> 00:09:49.722
And I think in any other time period,

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:50.890
what's been happening in the West

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:51.991
Bank, what's been happening with

00:09:51.991 --> 00:09:52.825
this deadly violence

00:09:52.825 --> 00:09:54.226
would be the top story.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.261
But then at the same time,

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.395
you have what's happening

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:57.930
on the streets, these massive protests

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:58.831
and also what's happening

00:09:58.831 --> 00:09:59.999
in the international arena.

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:00.533
Keep in mind,

00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:02.034
Benjamin Netanyahu has not been invited

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.603
to the US or the UAE just yet.

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.605
And Saudi and Iran, of course,

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:07.840
which complicates it even more. Exactly.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:08.140
I mean,

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.542
and I think that goes to show you

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.210
the sensitive balancing act

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:11.677
that Benjamin

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:12.979
Netanyahu needs to have right now,

00:10:12.979 --> 00:10:14.113
because not only is

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:15.548
he facing these international fronts,

00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:16.616
but domestically,

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:17.883
he needs to keep these right

00:10:17.883 --> 00:10:19.518
wing blocs as part of his coalition

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.153
otherwise he's not in power. Okay.

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:22.521
But the question

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:24.657
or the comment I hear most often

00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:26.525
is that the tail wagging the dog

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:27.393
that Benjamin

00:10:27.393 --> 00:10:28.194
Netanyahu said,

00:10:28.194 --> 00:10:30.296
I will control the coalition,

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:30.830
but actually

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.164
the coalition is controlling him.

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:33.232
And I think a big test

00:10:33.232 --> 00:10:34.467
and that maybe the true test will be

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:35.868
what's going to happen

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:37.536
next week with Ramadan coming,

00:10:37.536 --> 00:10:38.437
with Passover coming,

00:10:38.437 --> 00:10:39.505
there's a lot of concern

00:10:39.505 --> 00:10:40.506
about security issues

00:10:40.506 --> 00:10:41.941
specifically in Jerusalem.

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:42.775
I think a lot of eyes

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:43.876
will be on Itamar Ben-gvir,

00:10:43.876 --> 00:10:45.645
the minister of national security.

00:10:45.645 --> 00:10:46.646
Will he be doing anything

00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:47.346
that potentially make

00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:48.748
the situation worse?

00:10:48.748 --> 00:10:49.548
And will Benjamin need to

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:50.850
now be able to control him?

